## Summary
Ethiopian athlete Kejelcha has reclaimed the world half marathon record. This achievement comes shortly after his record-breaking marathon debut in London, where he finished in 1:59:40, the fastest debut marathon time ever recorded.

## Key Points
- Kejelcha retakes the world half marathon record.
- His marathon debut in London set a new record.
- The marathon debut time of 1:59:40 is the fastest ever recorded.


